URL: https://JuwelRana19.github.io/tvcQGComp,
    https://github.com/JuwelRana19/tvcQGComp
BugReports: https://github.com/JuwelRana19/tvcQGComp/issues
Description: G-computation for time-varying mixture exposures using
    quantile-based intervention levels. This approach estimates marginal
    effects corresponding to the expected change in the outcome given a joint
    intervention on all quantized time-varying mixture exposures across all
    time points. The package supports Monte Carlo skeleton generation,
    automatic lag-history creation, natural course prediction, static
    intervention simulation, pooled person-time or final-risk meta models, and
    cluster bootstrap confidence intervals. Works with survival outcomes.
    Reference: Juwel Rana, Alexander P. Keil, Hong Chen, Chen Chen,
    Marianne Hatzopoulou, Jad Zalzal, Tarik Benmarhnia, and Jay S. Kaufman.
    Joint Causal Effects of Time-Varying Traffic-Related Air Pollution
    Mixtures on Nonaccidental Mortality and Environmental Justice
    Implications: A Population-Based Cohort Study in Toronto, Canada.
